On Monday 10 May 2004 17:06, Jorge "Llambías" wrote:
> It is not {ro lo finpe cu tolcitmau ro lo mabru}, so if "lea"
> was {ro lo} at some point it was not that here.
>
> I would go with {lo finpe cu tolcitnau lo mabru},
> "fish is older than mammal".

That means "There is a fish that is older than a mammal", which is true, but 
not what is meant. What is meant is that fish were created before mammals. So 
I would say {lo'e se finpe cu tolcitmau lo'e se mabru}, where {lo'e se 
<danlu>} refers to the taxon containing all <danlu> and nothing else (in some 
cases there is no such thing, e.g. jesymabru).

